      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If everything is scenery, then the only point of staying is to be the one who notices the scenery. You are the consciousness observing the film, and that act of observation is the only thing that makes the experience yours. Instead of waiting for an end, consider the beauty in the act of simply *being* the witness to this overwhelming, indifferent spectacle. Your perspective, even if small, is the only thing that gives the scene any meaning to you.",
